From 928715ad1cef370951806f141fa110276afa149b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dwong <dowling.wong@kit.edu>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 18:33:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] T22: narrowband TIDMAD runner, tests and the frozen run
 archive

Runner experiments/mlst2026/t22_tidmad_narrowband.py with the representation
module tidmad_band.py; the T10-T12 endpoint module is imported unchanged, so the
only thing that changes is the space the rank-2 subspace is fitted in.  The
stage-0 protocol JSON (in the manuscript repository) is the single configuration
source: the runner derives the allocation offsets and asserts them against it.

Stages executed once each against /ceph/dwong/paper1_dataset/tidmad/raw:
characterize (11 stretches, calibration windows only, every instrument file
hashed), development (176 fits; re-scored once under amendment A4 with identical
contrasts), freeze (B = 9, b_eval = 32, b_cal = 8, dependence INCONCLUSIVE),
validation (24 fits, 0012/0013/0014), final test (40 fits, 0015-0019).  240 of a
250 fit cap.

Result: the learned rank-2 reconstruction moves from the trivial-predictor level
at the whole window (RMSE 0.655 vs zero 0.654, bin read 0.246) to below the bin
read in the band (0.249 vs 0.261), confirming the dimensional hypothesis in
direction.  All three verdicts are INCONCLUSIVE: the frozen dependence
assessment did not stabilise and the rule declared before development withholds
every benefit verdict.  The metric contribution is absent (-3.8e-05
[-2.3e-04, +1.3e-04], p = 0.70) -- in a nine-bin band the noise PSD is nearly
flat (in-band dynamic range 1.2-4.7 against 4.8e4 whole-window), so the
restriction that fixes estimation removes most of the metric's leverage.

31 implementation tests pass.  Draw arrays for both hold-out stages are archived
so every interval and p-value can be recomputed without the instrument data.

